 ite keeps the rules on file until they are finalized and until the Secreta
 ry of State website is updated to reflect the changes. The MaineCare Benef
 its Manual is available on-line at the\nSecretary of State’s website\n.\
 nBelow\, please find a MaineCare Notice of Agency Rulemaking Proposal. You
  can access the complete rule at\nhttp://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/rules/inde
 x.shtml.\n________________________________________________________________
 ____________\nNotice of Agency Rulemaking Proposal\nAgency:\nDepartment of
  Health and Human Services\, Office of MaineCare Services\, Division of Po
 licy\nChapter Number and Rule Title:\n10-144 C.M.R. Ch. 101\, MaineCare Be
 nefits Manual (MBM) Ch. II\, Sec. 20\, Home and Community Based Services f
 or Adults with Other Related Conditions\nType of Rule:\nRoutine Technical\
 nBrief Summary:\nThis Section 20 rule regulates home and community-based s
 ervices (HCBS) that are authorized by a federal Medicaid Section 1915(c) H
 CBS waiver that meets federal standards. MBM Ch. II\, Sec. 20 authorizes M
 aineCare HCBS waiver services for adults with conditions other than autism
  spectrum disorder that are related to but distinguishable from intellectu
 al disabilities. Through this rulemaking the Department proposes to: align
  similar processes\, new services\, service descriptions\, definitions\, a
 nd provider requirements with Maine’s four other Section 1915(c) waivers
 \; make\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/maine
 care-notice-agency-rule-making-proposal-mainecare-benefits-manual-chapter-
 ii-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 notice-agency-rule-making-proposal-mainecare-benefits-manual-chapter-ii-11
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d8bfedc50f7788b9@role-securities-financial.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T131500Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine DEP Initiates Legal Action Against Mall
 inckrodt US LLC to Address Cleanup Failures at Orrington Site
DESCRIPTION:Maine DEP Initiates Legal Action Against Mallinckrodt US LLC t
 o Address Cleanup Failures at Orrington Site\nMaine Department of Environm
 ental Protection sent this bulletin at 08/25/2026 03:45 PM EDT\n--- PRESS 
 RELEASE ---\nFor Immediate Release\nMaine DEP Initiates Legal Action Again
 st Mallinckrodt US LLC to Address Cleanup Failures at Orrington Site\nAUGU
 STA\, August 25\, 2026\n— The Department of Environmental Protection (DE
 P) filed a formal complaint today in Penobscot County Superior Court again
 st Mallinckrodt US LLC (Mallinckrodt). The complaint details the failure b
 y Mallinckrodt to complete cleanup of the former Holtrachem site located a
 long the Penobscot River in Orrington\, Maine\, one of Maine’s most cont
 aminated sites. Mallinckrodt has not met the remediation standards require
 d in the DEP’s 2008 Designation of Uncontrolled Hazardous Substance Site
  and Order\, that was affirmed in 2010 by the Board of Environmental Prote
 ction (BEP) in its own slightly modified order\, affirmed in 2012 by the M
 aine Business and Consumer Docket\, and finally affirmed in 2014 by the Ma
 ine Supreme Judicial Court sitting as the Law Court.\nThe former Holtrache
 m site was a chloralkali manufacturing facility\, which made chemicals com
 monly used in the pulp and paper industry. Historic operations resulted in
  a significant amount of contamination\, including highly toxic mercury an
 d chloropicrin\, in surrounding soils\, groundwaters\, and the Penobscot R
 iver. Site-specific standards were established by the DEP and BEP Orders t
 o ensure that the site would be cleaned up in a manner that would protect 
 public health\, safety\, and the environment.  Despite these Orders\, lar
 ge areas of soils still remain on site that exceed the site-specific clean
 up standards.\nThe DEP has worked diligently to provide oversight during c
 leanup of the former Holtrachem site to ensure that Mallinckrodt conducts 
 remediation in compliance with the DEP and BEP Orders. While progress has 
 been made\, it began to slow down as early as\nhttps://content.govdelivery
 .com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/426b2e7
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/426b2e7
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:011f4bed9fcdbb25@role-securities-financial.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T131500Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] September 2026
DESCRIPTION:O&M Newsletter\, September 2026\nMaine Department of Environme
 ntal Protection sent this bulletin at 08/25/2026 02:15 PM EDT\nSEPTEMBER 2
 026\nIn this issue:\nProtect your Plant with Free Cybersecurity Vulnerabil
 ity Assessments.\nRulemaking for Chapter 579.\nDMR-QA 2026 Update.\nShare 
 Your Knowledge - Consider Teaching a Class.\nMicroscopic Evaluations – A
  Tool for Process Control.\nTraining Highlights.\nFor Practice.\nProtect y
 our Plant with Free Cybersecurity Vulnerability Assessments.\nWith a rash 
 of cyber threats around the country\, it is a good time to verify that you
 r system is protected.\nFortunately\, there are several FREE options avail
 able for POTWs. The EPA and Maine National Guard (MENG) offer no-cost vuln
 erability assessments to POTWs.\nClick\nHere\nfor more information on EPA
 ’s vulnerability assessment program.\nPlease contact\nkevin.l.moncrieffe
 .mil@army.mil\nif you would like to know more about MENG cyber assessments
 .\nThe Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) offers Vulner
 ability and Web Application Scanning. Organizations typically reduce their
  risk and exposure by 40% within the first 12 months of these services. Cl
 ick\nHere\nfor more information on CISA Cyber Hygiene Services.\nIn additi
 on\, Maine Rural Water Association (MRWA) has partnered with DEF CON\nFran
 klin\nto offer FREE cybersecurity technical assistance to small communitie
 s.\nFranklin\n's\ncyber volunteers are highly qualified to help you scope
  your cyber needs\, identify existing vulnerabilities\, and patch up any w
 eaknesses. Over the past year\, the program has assisted small and rural w
 ater systems in Arizona\, Idaho\, Indiana\, Utah\, Oregon\, and Vermont\, 
 and is now expanding its services to the state of Maine. The initiative is
  named the\nProject Franklin\,\nin honor of US founding father Benjamin Fr
 anklin. Please contact Aaron Gaylord with MRWA\,\naaron.gaylord@mainerwa.o
 rg\nfor more information.\nAll services are completely voluntary and confi
 dential with no information shared with regulatory authorities.\nRule\nhtt
 ps://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/425e035
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/425e035
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
